===== Multiple processes =====

Multiple processes often apply simultaneously. An example of both insertion and deletion working together comes from the phrase {{IPA|/il bint kibiːra/}} ('the girl is grown up'):
Example of insertion and deletion together:
*Underlying representation: {{IPA|/il bint kibiːra/}}
*Epenthesis in CCC sequence: {{IPA|*/il bintekibiːra/}}
*Deletion of {{IPA|/i/}} VCVCV: {{IPA|[il bintekbiːra]}}
*Surface realization: {{IPA|[el ˈben.tekˈbiːræ]}}
Compare {{IPA|/il walad kibiːr/}} ('the boy is grown up'), where neither process applies.

Similarly, an example of both deletion and long-vowel shortening appears in the phrase {{IPA|/sˤaːħiba/}} ('friend' fem.):
*Underlying representation: {{IPA|/sˤaːħiba/}}
*Deletion of {{IPA|/i/}} in VCVCV: {{IPA|*/sˤaːħba/}}
*Vowel shortening in VCC: {{IPA|[sˤaħb+a]}}
*Surface realization: {{IPA|[ˈsˤɑħbɑ]}}
Compare with Classical Arabic {{IPA|/sˤaːħiba/}}.

The operation of the various processes can often produce ambiguity:
* {{IPA|/ana ʕaːwiz aːkul/}} → {{IPA|/ana ʕawzaːkul/}} ('I [masc.] want to eat')
* {{IPA|/ana ʕaːwiza aːkul/}} → {{IPA|/ana ʕawza aːkul/}} → {{IPA|/ana ʕawzaːkul/}} ('I [fem.] want to eat')
Hence, {{IPA|[ænæ ˈʕawˈzæːkol]}} is ambiguous in regards to grammatical gender.

